@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Machine Learning — Level-1 Primer Map (pre-LLM foundations)
' Index of the machine-learning families; each child carries its own confirmed source
' Level:  1

actor "Human expert" as H

package "Supervised — fit a function to labels" {
  component "svm/\nmargins + kernels" as SVM <<app>>
  component "trees-and-ensembles/\nbagging, boosting" as TREE <<app>>
  component "neural-networks/\ndepth + backprop" as NN <<app>>
}

package "Unsupervised — no labels" {
  component "clustering-and-dimred/\nk-means, PCA, embeddings" as UNS <<host>>
}

package "Learning from outcomes" {
  component "reinforcement-learning/\nTD, Q-learning, self-play" as RL <<host>>
}

package "Decide under uncertainty" {
  component "game-search/\nminimax, MCTS / UCT" as GS <<host>>
  component "imperfect-information-games/\nbelief, CFR, determinization" as III <<cloud>>
}

package "Machinery every family needs" {
  component "optimization/\ngradient + black-box search" as OPT <<async>>
  component "rating-systems/\nElo, Glicko, error bars" as RATE <<db>>
}

H ARROW_MAIN SVM
H ARROW_MAIN TREE
H ARROW_MAIN NN
H ARROW_MAIN UNS
H ARROW_MAIN RL
H ARROW_MAIN GS
H ARROW_MAIN III
H ARROW_MAIN RATE : start here — nothing else\nis falsifiable without it
H ARROW_MAIN OPT : then make the constants\na searchable vector

SVM ARROW_OPTIONAL OPT
NN ARROW_MAIN OPT : gradients
RL ARROW_MAIN OPT
GS ARROW_OPTIONAL III : tree assumption breaks
RL ARROW_OPTIONAL RATE : is the new policy stronger?
RATE ARROW_MAIN OPT : supplies the fitness signal\nblack-box search needs

note bottom of RATE
  **Why Level 1.** These are the practitioner's own
  craft — the same slot as ""../computer-science/"" —
  not prompts (L2), not a scaffold around a frozen
  model (L4), not weight updates to a pretrained one
  (L5-L6). Authored as primers, so they sit on the
  ladder floor.
  ----
  **Reading order for a measured build:**
  ""rating-systems/"" first (nothing else is
  falsifiable without it), then ""optimization/"" to
  make hand-tuned constants a searchable vector,
  then ""game-search/"" and
  ""imperfect-information-games/"" for lookahead, and
  only then a learned evaluator from
  ""neural-networks/"" + ""reinforcement-learning/"".
  ----
  ""../rag/"" is a sibling, not a child: those are
  LLM-era retrieval architectures, not pre-LLM ML.
end note
@enduml
